PDF Master document scanner: third-party notices
=================================================

The code in this folder is PDF Master's own, derived from open-doc-scanner
(MIT) with memory-only changes: the text model runs in row strips, ONNX
Runtime's memory arena is off, and the thread count and model folder come
from SCANNER_THREADS and SCANNER_MODELS. Output pixels are the same. The
models it runs and parts of its code come from these projects, each under
its own terms. Model files are pinned by size and SHA-256 in
models.json; all but text_sr_x3.onnx are fetched when the image is built
(scripts/fetch_scanner_models.py) and are not part of this repository.

DocAligner (page detection)
  Source:   https://github.com/DocsaidLab/DocAligner (pip package docaligner-docsaid)
  Licence:  Apache License 2.0, LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt. Copyright DocsaidLab.
  Files:    fastvit_sa24_h_e_bifpn_256_fp32.onnx (heatmap model) and
            lcnet050_p_multi_decoder_l3_d64_256_fp32.onnx (point model),
            unmodified, mirrored as release assets of
            github.com/shahzodjonweb/document-platform (tag scanner-models-1).
  Code:     aligner.py adapts DocAligner's preprocessing (a bilinear resize to
            256x256, CHW, float32 / 255) and runs the networks with ONNX
            Runtime in place of the docaligner-docsaid and capybara-docsaid
            packages. Modified: rewritten; no weight download, no GPU runtime.

